LICENSE — NOT YET CHOSEN
========================

The licence for the EOS CLI has not been decided yet. This file is a placeholder and is
not a grant of rights.

Until a licence is published here, the default applies: copyright is retained and no
permission is given to use, copy, modify or distribute this software. The source is
visible so that the publish protocol has a readable reference implementation, and so that
anyone can verify what the tool does with their repository — which are the two things that
matter most before you run something over your own code.

**Practically, this means:**

- Read it, audit it, and run it against your own repositories: that is what it is here for.
- Do not vendor it, fork it into a product, or redistribute it until a licence exists.
- If you need certainty before depending on this, open an issue and say so. A licence
  question from a real user is the fastest way to get one chosen.

A placeholder is uncomfortable and it is more honest than picking a licence badly. Choosing
one is easy to do and hard to undo — an open-source licence, once published, cannot be
withdrawn from the versions that carried it.

